  "description": "Block J, 431 Castleforbes Square offers an exceptional opportunity to rent a beautifully two-bedroom, one-bathroom apartment located in the heart of Dublin’s vibrant North Docklands — one of the city’s most dynamic and desirable urban quarters.\n\nPositioned on the fourth floor of this well-maintained development, the west facing property has been stylishly refurbished throughout, offering a sophisticated blend of contemporary design, comfort, and practicality. Every detail has been considered — from premium finishes and sleek sound proof flooring to elegant lighting and bespoke fittings — creating a home of true quality\n\nThe bright, open-plan living and dining space enjoys generous proportions and large windows that flood the interior with natural light. A high-specification kitchen features integrated appliances, ample storage, and fine worktops.\n\nBoth double bedrooms are beautifully appointed, with slide wardrobes and wooden floors.  The family bathroom is partially tiled with a bath and sanitary ware.\n\nThe property is completed by a laundry closets in the hallway.\n\nHallway - 7sqm\nWooden floors, intercom, access to all rooms\n\nLiving/dining room - 20sqm\nWooden floors, new radiator, bespoke light fittings, access to 6sqm west facing balcony \n\nKitchen - 6sqm\nFully renovated, integrated units, tiled backsplash\n\nMaster bedroom - 12sqm\nWooden floor, built-in slide wardrobe.  \n\n2nd double bedroom - 11sqm\nWooden floor, built-in slide wardrobe.  \n\nFamily bathroom - 4sqm\nPartially tiled, bath, WHB, WC\n\nLaundry closet - 3sqm\nWashing machine, storage\n\nStorage closet - 1.5sqm\n\nPerfectly positioned in Dublin’s Docklands, this apartment is moments from the IFSC, Spencer Dock, and Grand Canal Dock — home to many of the world’s leading tech and financial firms. A host of cafés, bars, restaurants, and leisure amenities are within walking distance, while excellent transport links include the LUAS, DART, and numerous Dublin Bus routes, offering effortless access to the wider city.",
